1. BUSINESS PROBLEM
    ==================================================

OCE is a large telecom order orchestration ecosystem involving hundreds of microservices, APIs, Kafka topics/events, command-based processing, Camunda orchestration, downstream systems, and other AT&T platforms such as OGCJ and fulfillment/warehouse systems.

When an order becomes stuck or fails, testing/support teams currently perform a largely manual investigation.

Typical request:

“Order <ORDER_ID> is stuck in OCE while processing Create Product Order. Please investigate and explain why.”

Today, a human investigator may need to:

1. Search audit logs.
2. Examine API requests and responses.
3. Determine which API/event was the last successful step.
4. Determine which step failed or was not triggered.
5. Search ELK logs using order ID/MDC/correlation information.
6. Examine Kafka/event processing.
7. Examine Camunda workflow state and gateway/precondition decisions.
8. Inspect source code to understand business conditions.
9. Search Wiki/documentation.
10. Understand service dependencies.
11. Consult the BSS Knowledge Graph.
12. Potentially consult TraceIQ.
13. Correlate all evidence.
14. Determine the root cause.
15. Explain the reason and recommended next action to the testing/support team.

The goal of OCE Insight is to automate as much of this investigation as safely and reliably possible.

